<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">7 July in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 7 July, from 1456 to 2005.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/joan-of-arc" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/joan-of-arc.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1456 CE <span class="tih-ago">570 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Joan of Arc is cleared of heresy 25 years after her death</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A retrial authorised by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-callixtus-iii">Pope Callixtus III</a> quashed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joan-of-arc">Joan of Arc</a>'s 1431 conviction and declared her innocent. She was canonised as a saint in 1920.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1777 CE <span class="tih-ago">249 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">American rearguard fights the British at Hubbardton</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Retreating from Fort Ticonderoga, an American rearguard fought pursuing British and German troops at Hubbardton, Vermont. Though defeated, they slowed Burgoyne's advance towards eventual surrender at Saratoga.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1898 CE <span class="tih-ago">128 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">President McKinley signs the resolution annexing Hawaii</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">McKinley signed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/newlands-resolution">Newlands Resolution</a>, annexing the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hawaii">Hawaii</a> five years after American businessmen had overthrown Queen Liliuokalani. Hawaii became a US territory and, in 1959, the 50th state.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1937 CE <span class="tih-ago">89 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Marco Polo Bridge Incident sparks war between China and Japan</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A night-time clash between Japanese and Chinese troops at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lugou-bridge">Marco Polo Bridge</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a> escalated into full-scale war. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-sino-japanese-war">Second Sino-Japanese War</a> merged into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> and cost millions of Chinese lives.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marco-polo">Marco Polo</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1985 CE <span class="tih-ago">41 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Boris Becker, 17, becomes Wimbledon's youngest men's champion</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Unseeded West German Boris Becker beat Kevin Curren in four sets to win Wimbledon at 17. He remains the youngest men's singles champion in the tournament's history.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">2005 CE <span class="tih-ago">21 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Suicide bombers kill 52 on London's transport network</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Four bombers struck three Underground trains and a bus during the morning rush hour, killing 52 people. It was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>'s deadliest terrorist attack since Lockerbie, a day after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> won the 2012 Olympics.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li></ol>
